    <title lang="en">THE LAUNCH OF CHANG'E 7</title>
    <desc lang="en">Broadcasting live from Hainan's Wenchang Launch Site, Phoenix Hong Kong Channel delivers continuous Cantonese-led coverage of China's ambitious Chang'e 7 lunar mission. The special program tracks the deployment of an orbiter, lander, rover, and specialized "hopping" probe as they head toward Shackleton Crater at the lunar south pole to map rugged terrain and hunt for sub-surface water ice. Alongside expert technical rundowns and real-time feeds, the coverage spotlights Hong Kong's local scientific contributions—focusing on the University of Hong Kong's (HKU) development of the ILO-C lunar camera payload. Ultimately, the broadcast frames Chang'e 7 as a pivotal stepping stone toward building the International Lunar Research Station (ILRS) and preparing for China's upcoming crewed lunar landing.</desc>
